# Build context exclusions.
#
# containers/Dockerfile CLONES the repository at a pinned ref rather than COPYing a context, so
# nothing here affects what ends up in the image. It matters anyway: `docker build .` uploads the
# whole context to the daemon before reading the Dockerfile, so without this a local build ships
# gigabytes it will never use -- .pixi alone is 3.3 GB of solved environments.
#
# It also guards the other direction. If anyone ever switches back to `COPY . /opt/pipeline`, these
# are the things that must not silently enter an image that gets pushed to a registry.

# Solved environments and caches -- rebuilt inside the image, 3.3 GB locally
.pixi/
.snakemake/

# Results and run artefacts. Never inputs to a build, and historically the largest thing here.
results/
results_bak/
RDA_objects/
work/
logs/
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*

# Generated test data: tests/data/ is gitignored and regenerated by src/make_test_data.R
tests/data/

# Version control and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.githooks/

# Documentation and paper material: not needed to run the pipeline
docs/
*.md
!README.md
